# Build trees (one per CMake preset)
/build/
compile_commands.json
CMakeUserPresets.json

# vcpkg
/vcpkg_installed/

# Generated flatc headers live in the build tree only and are never committed
# (rule R3). Belt and braces in case someone points flatc at the source tree.
**/generated/

# Emscripten output
*.wasm
*.wasm.map

# Experiment output — CSVs are committed deliberately (see docs/EVALUATION.md),
# but scratch runs and rendered charts are not.
/results/scratch/
/results/**/*.png
/results/**/*.svg
# Rendered previews are DERIVED — `render-preview` regenerates them from a
# committed scene and a fixed seed, so the repo carries the recipe, not the
# output (CONVENTIONS.md §11).
/results/**/*.ppm
# Dotfile scratch from experiment drivers — intermediate, not evidence.
/results/.*

# Generated scene assets (regenerated by script, never committed)
/assets/generated/

# Local coordinator state
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# Fuzzing artifacts. NOTE: fuzz/corpus/ is deliberately NOT ignored — seeds
# are committed evidence (docs/CONVENTIONS.md §7 T4, EVALUATION.md E8).
crash-*
leak-*
timeout-*
oom-*
/fuzz/artifacts/

# Secrets and local config
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# NOTE: do NOT add `*.md` here. An earlier revision did, which silently
# excluded CLAUDE.md, RESEARCH.md, and all of docs/ from version control —
# i.e. the entire handoff surface this repo depends on (RISKS.md R-E).

*.md
!README.md
fuzz/dist/

# `results/` IS NOT IGNORED, and a blanket rule for it used to sit here.
#
# It silently overrode the careful carve-out above — the one whose comment says
# "CSVs are committed deliberately (see docs/EVALUATION.md)". Measured
# 2026-08-07: 23 of 49 files in results/ were tracked, and the 23 only because
# someone had force-added them. Among the missing were BOTH raw data files from
# the borrowed-machine session — the only NVIDIA measurements in existence, and
# what G4's cross-vendor determinism claim rests on.
#
# THIRD TIME THIS SHAPE HAS APPEARED: fuzz/corpus/ ignored while the logs
# reported half a billion executions, `*.md` once excluding the entire handoff
# surface, and now this. In each case a BROAD rule silently defeated a NARROW
# intent stated in a comment a few lines away. A comment is not a rule.
#
# `*.md` above still excludes results/*.md, which is deliberate and separate.

# fuzz/corpus/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It IS the regression net: CI replays
# every committed seed with -runs=0 on each push, and R11 states outright that
# the corpus is committed.
#
# It was ignored until 2026-08-06, and 125 protocol seeds only existed in git
# because someone once force-added them. Every entry found since — 295 from the
# 4.12 campaign, plus the entire 4.13 asset corpus — was silently dropped, so
# CI's net was frozen at the original seeds while the logs reported half a
# billion executions. Same shape as the `*.md` mistake noted above: an ignore
# rule quietly excluding the thing it was protecting.